  "caveats": [
    "This is a controlled reduced-model replication, not a full-resolution reproduction of the published DNS.",
    "No measured dye profile or dye-depth series is included; dye comparisons are between matched numerical cases.",
    "Wind and extra-loss coefficients were fitted to the 15\u201320 s wave interval; later wave observations are held out.",
    "Measured characteristic slope contains the full surface; plotted simulation slope contains parent modes only.",
    "A finite initial Gaussian dye layer of fixed physical width is used on every grid; no evolution clipping or mass renormalization.",
    "Two grid spacings provide a resolution sensitivity check, not a formal convergence demonstration.",
    "Gaussian current noise has the same seed and RMS on both grids, but its spatial realization changes with the grid; refinement differences also include this perturbation sensitivity.",
    "Prognostic parents retain nine free modes with linear intrinsic evolution; nonlinear parent wave-wave interactions are omitted.",
    "More than 5% of parent action on either retained-band boundary flags possible spectral truncation; inspect the boundary-action checks before interpreting dye differences.",
    "Cho remains one-way and does not directly transport the mean-model dye or deposit turbulence.",
    "A clean validity stop is partial scientific output, not completion of the target interval.",
    "The initial coefficients were estimated from wave data over 15\u201320 s. That interval is calibration, not independent validation; later wave data provide a held-out comparison.",
    "No laboratory dye profiles are included. Dye comparisons here are among matched numerical experiments.",
    "Cho remains a one-way disturbance calculation. Its damping and the empirical parent-loss coefficient are distinct.",
    "Empirical wind and loss rates change the full parent amplitude history but are excluded from the intrinsic boundary residual used to force Cho; no explicit aerodynamic pressure forcing is added.",
    "The wind input is reduced when its wave-momentum demand exceeds the supplied stress. The limiter is recorded; it is a budget bound, not a fitted coefficient.",
    "A trajectory that reaches the declared parent-band steepness limit of 0.35 stops there and is not a complete matched benchmark.",
    "This first 3 cm benchmark uses linear intrinsic evolution with a narrow nine-mode parent band and carrier-self surface reconstruction; near-resonant broad-band cubic dynamics are excluded.",
    "Momentum retains WENO5 advection with first-order upwind fallback at boundaries. Dye adds a common-face flux limiter around the native WENO donor reconstruction; adjacent cells share the same limited flux, and cell concentrations are not clipped.",
    "The native RK3 time integrator is not SSP, so the dye flux limiter is not a strict positivity guarantee. Dye mass and negative-concentration checks remain active.",
    "Numerical completion and budget checks do not establish physical validity or resolution convergence."
  ],
